//  BEACON ICON SHEETS -- ONE IMAGE, TWO STATES.
//
//  Every beacon icon in this folder is a 32x16 sheet: frame "on" at x=0 with a
//  green status dot, frame "off" at x=16 with a red one.
//
//  WHY A SHEET RATHER THAN TWO FILES. An activeitem's INVENTORY ICON is
//  rendered from its animation, and global tags substitute into the part image
//  live -- so `<partImage>:<state>` plus animator.setGlobalTag("state", ...)
//  changes the icon with no item parameter, no rebuild, and therefore no effect
//  on stacking. Copied from vanilla's relocator, which shows its stored-creature
//  count exactly this way.
//
//  This is why swapping the inventoryIcon STRING does nothing: nothing reads it
//  after the animation exists.
{
	"frameGrid" : {
		"size" : [16, 16],
		"dimensions" : [2, 1],
		"names" : [
			[ "on", "off" ]
		]
	}
}
